\section{What is written where}{

Every save is appended to the journal FIRST (the source of truth, read by
\code{\link[=landmark_journal_read]{landmark_journal_read()}} and \code{\link[=consolidate_landmarks]{consolidate_landmarks()}} together with the
journals written by the old Rfishmorph digitizer), then to the working
copy of the workbook (\code{out_path}), edited in place through openxlsx and
written atomically every \code{xlsx_flush_every} records. The journal \code{row_key}
is the species name (\code{"reconstruct"}, \code{"correct"}) or the photograph file
name (\code{"new"}), as before, so the history of a species continues across the
two tools. The quality score is on the common scale, 1 (unusable) to
5 (excellent), empty when not scored.
